course: dictionary
lesson: 5709
title: Lonesome: alone and far from others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lonesome means sad because you are alone, with no friends or company. «Lonesome George, the last tortoise of his kind from Pinta Island, died in 2012.» Read the clues: he was the last of his kind, so there was no other tortoise like him. Lonesome points to being alone, with no others of his kind near him.
explain: Lonesome can also describe a place. «A lonesome road» is far from other people, empty and quiet. Ask yourself: is the word about a feeling, or about a place? The words around it will tell you.
explain: In American and Canadian talk, «I'm lonesome» means «I'm lonely». In the UK, «on your lonesome» is informal and means all alone. The word is mostly American, so a dictionary helps if you are unsure.
fact: Lonesome means sad because you are alone, or far from other people.
fact: «Lonesome George» was the last tortoise of his kind from Pinta Island, and he died in 2012.
fact: A lonesome road is empty and quiet, with no other people near.
fact: Lonesome is mostly used in American English, and you will often hear it in songs and cowboy tales.
fact: Lonely is a close synonym for lonesome, so you can often swap one for the other.
exercise: «Lonesome George, the last tortoise of his kind from Pinta Island, died in 2012.» What does lonesome mean here? | Very old and wise | Angry with the people of Pinta Island | Fast and strong | *Sad because he was alone, with no others of his kind
exercise: «The lonesome road ran past empty fields for miles.» What does lonesome describe? | *A road far from other people, empty and quiet | A road full of cars and noise | A road that is newly painted | A road that is very wide
exercise: Which word means the same as lonesome in the sense of sad because you are alone? | Happy | Loud | Hungry | *Lonely
test: «Kim said, "I'm lonesome," when her friends went home.» What does Kim mean? | She is angry with her friends | *She is sad because she is alone | She is hungry | She is very tired from running
test: «Sam walked to school on his lonesome.» What does on his lonesome mean? | Carrying a heavy bag | Very quickly | *All alone | Together with his friends
exam: Which sentence uses lonesome to mean far from other people? | *The lonesome road ran past empty fields for miles | The class sang a lonesome song together | Lonesome George ate a big lunch | The lonesome bell rang loudly
